Come to think of it, with all the filtering going on in so many=20
softwares these days adding it to Nethack would not be too bad an idea.
Let's say you could press CTRL F and the last message would never=20
appear again.
The hard way to do this would be to dismiss that particular message=20
each time it appears but that would probably mean adding a lot of code=20
where the messages are generated (i.e. in several source files).
The easy way would be to take that message, maybe analyze it a bit and=20
store the result in a buffer. For each message after that, check for a=20
match and possibly discard the new message. There's a possibility of=20
error here but it should be fairly easy to implement and most=20
errorenous discards are very likely CTRL F candidates anwyay.

